; PgBouncer credentials. Copy to pgbouncer-userlist.txt and fill in.
;
;   cp infra/pgbouncer-userlist.txt.example infra/pgbouncer-userlist.txt
;   chmod 600 infra/pgbouncer-userlist.txt
;
; SCRAM verifiers, not passwords. Postgres already stores one per role, so copy
; it rather than writing a second plaintext copy of the database password onto
; the same disk:
;
;   docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U leadflow -tAc \
;     "SELECT '\"'||rolname||'\" \"'||rolpassword||'\"' FROM pg_authid WHERE rolname = 'master_saas_app'"
;
; Only the application role belongs here. Migrations and administration connect
; to Postgres directly (see the note in docker-compose.pgbouncer.yml), so the
; owning role has no reason to be reachable through the pooler.
"master_saas_app" "SCRAM-SHA-256$4096:...
